==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from the process of [[pan#Verb|panning]] for gold:
* '''1872''', [[w:Mark Twain|Mark Twain]], ''Roughing It'', ch. 61:
*: "Prospecting" is hunting for a "placer"; "indications" are signs of its presence; "'''panning out'''" refers to the washing process by which the grains of gold are separated from the dirt.

===Verb===
{{infl|en|verb|head=[[to]] [[pan]] [[out]]}}

#{{idiom}} To [[succeed]]; to [[proceed]] according to [[plan]]; to [[result]] or [[end up]].
#:''His plans to get rich in the stock market never seem to '''pan out''' the way he imagines.''

